    "description": "Technical lead for JMARS, a simple GIS and the principle mission planning system for NASA's Mars THEMIS and HiRISE cameras, and the Lunar LROC camera.  Development was in C++ and Java, and Bash/Perl/Python scripting languages.  The work involved raster and vector data ingestion, server maintenance, adjudication of authentication issues, software release testing, design of new functionality, charting the product coarse for JMARS, and implementation of new features for the JMARS client, the WMS server, and various ancillary services.  The system as a whole processed terabytes of NASA data every year.",
